      "message": "1. unsigned char (or just u8)?\n2. We must make sure the address, not just the size, is page-aligned?\n3. With the existing PAGE_SIZE-aligned `union pkvm_pv_param` with explicitly listed possible params, we have an assurance that any used param will fit into this memory region (so in particular, in principle it might even exceed one page, and it\u0027s still gonna work just fine). Whereas with this new interface, the caller needs to take care not to exceed PAGE_SIZE.\n\\\nSo maybe there\u0027s nothing wrong in keeping all possible params (including iommu-specific structures) defined in a centralized place in `union pkvm_pv_param` instead?",
